# Silhouette (CR 615.1, 120.2b): "Choose target creature. If a spell or ability that targets that creature would cause a source to
# deal damage to that creature this turn, prevent that damage." On Bot2's turn 4 Bot2 casts Bite Down, its Hill Giant (3/3) to deal
# 3 damage to Bot1's Aegis Turtle (0/5); Bot1 answers with Silhouette on its own Turtle (a player is no creature to choose). The
# Giant is the source, Bite Down the spell that targets the Turtle and causes the damage: all 3 is prevented. Bot2's Pyroclasm then
# deals 2 damage to each creature without targeting: that is not prevented, so the Turtle ends with 2 damage - 5, and dead, had
# Bite Down's not been prevented; 0 had the effect prevented all damage to it.

